# SEO work uses seo-audit-kit

When the task is SEO for this site, use the installed package. Do not write a new crawler or audit script for a check the package already runs.

The command is `npx seokit`, from this repo. The site is `https://byteforce.ma`. Language is `fr`.

```bash
npx seokit audit https://byteforce.ma --lang fr
npx seokit page https://byteforce.ma/path --lang fr
npx seokit content https://byteforce.ma --lang fr
npx seokit explain CHECK_ID
npx seokit diff
```

PageSpeed only when the user asks for it: `npx seokit audit https://byteforce.ma --psi`. The key is the `PSI_KEY` environment variable. If the API returns 429, say the quota is used up. Do not invent a score.

Reports go to `seokit-report/`. Do not commit that folder unless the user asks.

The tool reads the HTML the server sends. It does not execute client-side JavaScript, and it does not measure rankings or search volume. Say that limit when a finding may be wrong because of it.
